      "worked": "Perpendicular gradients satisfy $m_1m_2=-1$, so $m_2=-\\frac1{m_1}$.\n\n$a:\\quad m_2=-\\frac1{\\frac{1}{2}}=-2$\n\n$b:\\quad m_2=-\\frac12$\n\n$c:\\quad m_2=-\\frac1{\\frac{4}{3}}=-\\frac34$\n\n$d:\\quad m_2=-\\frac13$\n\n$e:\\quad m_2=-\\frac1{-\\frac{3}{4}}=\\frac43$\n\n$f:\\quad m_2=-\\frac1{-5}=\\frac15$\n\n$g:\\quad m_2=-\\frac1{-\\frac{1}{2}}=2$\n\n$h:\\quad m_2=-\\frac1{\\frac{2}{3}}=-\\frac32$",
